// TEST: Sqrt Inexact Magnitude Rejects (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3006
// ERROR-CONTAINS: no exact square root in the unit scale grammar
// Even dims are not enough: the MAGNITUDE has to have an exact square root
// too. 4047 is not a perfect square, so sqrt(acre) is 63.6... * meters -- a
// factor no exact rational-times-constants scale can hold. Unit algebra
// never rounds (a rounded factor lands in a TYPE, where no later check can
// catch it), so this refuses and names the fix: declare the unit as a square.
Unit meters
Unit acre = 4047 * meters ^ 2
let plot: Float<acre> = 4.0
let bad = sqrt(plot)
